WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.920
Horror icons, primetime stars, criminals,
and queens: the cast of The Craft has done

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:06.990
it all.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:10.440
Want to know which breakout performer captured
Ben Stiller’s heart?

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.639
Wondering why you recognized the pilot from
Sharknado?

00:00:13.639 --> 00:00:16.780
Keep watching to learn all about this ensemble
cast!

00:00:17.818 --> 00:00:22.849
Sarah Bailey, played by Robin Tunney, is a
bit unsure of herself, and not just because

00:00:22.849 --> 00:00:25.380
she recently transferred to a new school.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:29.190
She doesn't know how or why she's able to
do the things she can, and fears she’ll

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:32.360
lose control of her powers and hurt the people
around her.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:37.510
Following The Craft, Tunney got another dose
of the supernatural in 1999’s iconically

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:39.120
bad End of Days.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:43.770
She plays the role of Christine York, a woman
whom the Devil, played by Gabriel Byrne, has

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:48.329
selected to be the mother of the antichrist
— unless Arnold Schwarzenegger has anything

00:00:48.329 --> 00:00:50.390
to say about it!

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:52.880
"Christine, come to me.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:55.100
I am the one you’ve been waiting for.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:58.399
I am the answer to your prayers."

00:00:58.399 --> 00:01:03.219
For 2000's critically panned Vertical Limit,
Tunney took on the role of Annie Garret, a

00:01:03.219 --> 00:01:07.770
trapped mountain climber in need of rescue
by her brother, played by Chris O’Donnell.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:13.290
Tunney later appeared in 2006's period crime
drama Hollywoodland, which told a fictionalized

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:18.330
version of the death of Superman actor George
Reeves, portrayed by Ben Affleck.

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:21.660
She plays Leonore Lemmon, Reeves' fiancee
at the time of his death.

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:27.100
In 2008, Tunney took up the role of Teresa
Lisbon, boss and love interest to the title

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:30.530
character on USA's procedural drama The Mentalist.

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:35.500
More recently, she had a lead role as Maya
Travis on ABC's ill-fated legal drama The

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:36.860
Fix.

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:41.800
Fairuza Balk plays the ambitious and spiteful
role of Nancy Downs.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:46.060
Unsatisfied by the insurance payout from her
late stepfather’s death, and jealous of

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:51.320
Sarah’s natural talent, Nancy goes to drastic
measures to strengthen her powers and outclass

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:52.470
her friends.

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:57.420
The same yearThe Craft hit theaters, Balk
washed off the goth makeup and popped in some

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:02.530
custom incisors for the role of human-cat
hybrid, Aissa in the remake of The Island

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:04.220
of Dr. Moreau.

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:08.360
Two years later, Balk brought to life another
complicated, power-hungry young woman for

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:11.000
1998's American History X.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:16.140
She played Stacey, the soon-to-be ex-girlfriend
of recently former Neo-Nazi skinhead, Derek

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:18.439
Vinyard, played by Edward Norton.

00:02:18.439 --> 00:02:23.430
The very same year, she took on the decidedly
lighter role of Vicki Vallencourt, love interest

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:28.129
to Adam’s Sandler’s character, Bobby Boucher,
in the sports comedy The Waterboy.

00:02:28.129 --> 00:02:34.260
In 2015, Balk landed a recurring role on the
Showtime drama Ray Donovan, playing Ginger,

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:37.170
a prostitute who befriends the title character's
father.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:41.780
In Amazon's series Paradise City, Balk plays
the role of Lizzie Thomas, the grandmother

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:45.819
to Faith, the daughter to series lead Johnny
Faust, played by Andy Biersack.

00:02:46.893 --> 00:02:51.239
Bonnie Harper, as played by actor Neve Campbell,
starts out on the quiet side.

00:02:51.239 --> 00:02:56.310
Covered in mysterious burn scars, she does
her best to hide as much of her body as possible.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:03:01.209
When Sarah shows up and the witches have their
fourth, she manages to remove her scars completely,

00:03:01.209 --> 00:03:05.019
and gains newfound confidence in her appearance
from then on.

00:03:05.019 --> 00:03:09.069
The Craft really put Campbell on the path
to being a '90s it-girl.

00:03:09.069 --> 00:03:13.879
The same year The Craft came out, she starred
as protagonist Sydney Prescott in Wes Craven’s

00:03:13.879 --> 00:03:19.400
teen horror flick, Scream. Campbell went on
to reprise the role for the 1997 sequel Scream

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:24.469
2, as well as 2000’s Scream 3 and 2011's
Scream 4.

00:03:24.469 --> 00:03:29.080
Following Craven’s death in 2015, Cambpell
also appeared in Scream 5, which came out

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:31.519
in January 2022.

00:03:31.519 --> 00:03:36.159
In addition to the teen horror film genre,
Campbell has also found success on the small

00:03:36.159 --> 00:03:37.159
screen.

00:03:37.159 --> 00:03:40.590
In the popular drama, Party of Five, she stars
as orphan Julia Salinger.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:45.609
She also enjoyed a recurring role as political
strategist LeeAnn Harvey on Netflix's political

00:03:45.609 --> 00:03:47.659
thriller drama House Of Cards.

00:03:48.572 --> 00:03:52.819
Rochelle Zimmerman, played by Rachel True,
rounds out the quartet of young witches.

00:03:52.819 --> 00:03:57.900
In addition to dabbling in witchcraft, she
is also a member of the school's diving team.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:01.560
Despite her diving talent, she’s bullied
relentlessly by her teammate, Laura.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:06.190
Laura's racist taunts lead Rochelle to seek
revenge, eventually causing the superficial

00:04:06.190 --> 00:04:09.500
pretty girl to lose her hair and become despondent.

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:13.989
Two years after filming The Craft, True joined
the cast of Half Baked.

00:04:13.989 --> 00:04:18.560
In the dim stoner comedy, she played the super
cleverly named Mary Jane Potman, opposite

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:21.450
Dave Chapelle’s character, Thurgood Jenkins.

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:24.790
Mary Jane is Thurgood’s love interest in
the film, eventually forcing him to choose

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:26.950
between sex or smoking weed.

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:28.310
"Marijuana is terrible.

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:30.230
It’s a gateway drug.

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:32.540
Everybody knows it leads to other stuff."

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:38.130
Beginning in 2002, True took on the role of
Mona Thorne in the UPN sitcom Half &amp; Half,

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:42.090
which followed the unexpected friendship between
Mona and her half-sister, Dee Dee, played

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:44.080
by Essence Atkins.

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:48.420
True appeared on the show throughout its entire
four-season run before it was canceled in

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:49.920
2006.

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:54.640
More recently, True appeared as Jonni Valentine
in Sharknado 2: The Second One.

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:59.430
True plays the first officer aboard Flight
209, a plane attacked by airborne sharks.

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:04.030
Unfortunately, she doesn’t last long.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:11.760
The same year, she appeared in Blood Lake:
Attack of the Killer Lampreys as Marcy, a

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:15.200
member of the fish and wildlife service who
falls prey to the title monsters.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:20.280
Actor Skeet Ulrich took on the role of the
repugnant Chris Hooker.

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:25.120
Like many archetypal campus kings, Chris maintains
a good guy persona when the occasion calls

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:30.080
for it, feigning innocence and side-stepping
the truth like an All-American running back.

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:33.700
When Chris doesn’t get what he wants, the
charm turns off and the mean-spirited bully

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:34.950
comes out.

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:39.330
Sarah manages to tame him with a love spell,
but this eventually backfires when Chris becomes

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:41.130
obsessed and dangerous.

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:45.830
Ulrich had a prolific run in the mid '90s,
with The Craft serving as one of his five

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:48.710
film appearances in 1996 alone.

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:52.700
Later that year, he joined co-star Neve Campbell
in the franchise-launching Scream, though

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:55.720
his character didn't enjoy the same longevity
as hers.

00:05:55.720 --> 00:06:00.890
Ulrich played Billy Loomis, Sydney Prescott's
boyfriend and initial murder suspect.

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:05.380
After revealing himself as one of the two
killers, alongside his friend and co-conspirator

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:08.980
Stu, played by Matthew Lillard, Sydney shoots
him in the head.

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:14.120
The actor went on to appear as Vincent, the
model-turned-assailant, in 1997's acclaimed

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:15.600
As Good as it Gets.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:21.090
Two decades later, Ulrich took up the role
of Forsythe Pendleton Jones II on the CW’s

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:22.090
Riverdale.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:26.190
Ulrich played the reformed criminal, father
to Jughead, and eventual Riverdale sheriff

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:29.260
for five seasons before departing the series.

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:31.300
In an interview with Variety, Ulrich stated,

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:34.340
“I’m leaving Riverdale because I got bored
creatively.”

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:40.000
Mitt, Chris’s slacker best friend, is brought
to life by actor Breckin Meyer.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.460
Mitt is goofy, but a loyal friend to Chris.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:47.490
He's seemingly got nothing but wisecracks
to offer, until he gets an eyeful of a scar-free

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:48.490
Bonnie, that is.

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:54.040
In 1998, Meyer appeared in 54 alongside fellow
'90s up-and-comer Ryan Phillippe, with the

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:57.510
two playing bartenders at the infamous New
York City hotspot.

00:06:57.510 --> 00:07:02.450
In 2000's sophomoric sex comedy Road Trip,
he landed the lead role of Josh Parker, a

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:06.440
man forced to travel across the country in
order to stop a sex tape he made with another

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:10.070
girl from being delivered to his long-distance
girlfriend.

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:14.850
The following year, Meyer played lawyer Nick
Schaffer in the 2001 comedy Rat Race, where

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:20.310
he competes in a race across the desert funded
by John Cleese’s character, Donald Sinclair.

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:25.890
On the small screen, Meyer played Jared Franklin,
one half of the title duo on Franklin &amp; Bash.

00:07:25.890 --> 00:07:30.870
Jared, an unorthodox lawyer, works alongside
his partner and long-time friend Peter Bash,

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:32.620
played by Mark-Paul Gosselaar.

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:38.080
Meyer also joined The Craft co-star Robin
Tunney in the 2019 legal drama The Fix, playing

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:40.250
the L.A. district attorney, Charlie Wiest.

00:07:41.427 --> 00:07:44.890
Laura Lizzie, played by Christine Taylor,
is kind of the worst.

00:07:44.890 --> 00:07:49.400
She's openly and unapologetically racist to
Rochelle, taunting the young woman and deriding

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:50.430
her hair.

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:51.430
From yelling "Shark!"

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:56.680
in the middle of Rochelle's dive to just all-around
nastiness, Laura's eventual comeuppance is

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:59.330
satisfying, if not a bit guilt-inducing.

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:03.310
Outside of her role in The Craft, we assume
Christine Taylor is perfectly nice.

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:06.090
Why else would Ben Stiller have married her
in 2000?

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:10.921
Taylor and Stiller would go on to appear in
2001's Zoolander and 2004's Dodgeball: A True

00:08:10.921 --> 00:08:12.340
Underdog Story.

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:16.310
In Zoolander, viewers will recognize Taylor
as the fictional TIME Magazine journalist

00:08:16.310 --> 00:08:21.580
Matilda Jeffries, whose hit-piece makes title
character Derek Zoolander look like a fool.

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:26.860
In Dodgeball, she portrays bank lawyer Kate
Veatch, where she dodges both balls and unwanted

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:29.610
advances from Stiller’s character, White
Goodman.

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:35.779
Taylor has a cameo in the 2008 action flick
satire, Tropic Thunder, appearing in the film-within-the-film,

00:08:35.779 --> 00:08:36.819
Simple Jack.

00:08:36.819 --> 00:08:42.649
Beginning in 2016, she took on the recurring
role of Gail in HBO’s series, Search Party.

00:08:42.649 --> 00:08:45.460
She plays the rich boss to Alia Shawkat’s
character, Dory.

00:08:46.819 --> 00:08:50.800
Spanish actress Assumpta Serna took on the
role of Lirio for The Craft.

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:55.680
Viewers first meet Lirio when Nancy and the
gang take Sarah to her bookstore and proceed

00:08:55.680 --> 00:09:01.120
to shoplift from it; Sarah surprises the spiritually
inclined shopkeeper by actually paying for

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:02.120
something.

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:05.589
The bulk of Serna's filmography has come in
international fare, though she has logged

00:09:05.589 --> 00:09:09.459
plenty of English-language projects in the
years since The Craft premiered.

00:09:09.459 --> 00:09:12.639
Among those is the 2003 TV movie, Henry VIII.

00:09:12.639 --> 00:09:17.920
She later appeared in the 2008 indie crime
drama Uncertainty, starring Joseph Gordon-Levitt

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:19.509
as the protagonist, Bobby.

00:09:19.509 --> 00:09:23.790
Serna appears as Sylvia Montero, mother to
Bobby’s pregnant girlfriend, Kate, played

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:24.790
by Lynn Collins.

00:09:25.829 --> 00:09:29.009
Actor Cliff De Young plays Sarah's father
in The Craft.

00:09:29.009 --> 00:09:33.329
While Sarah has a complicated relationship
with her father, she’s relieved to discover

00:09:33.329 --> 00:09:37.760
he’s still alive despite what Bonnie, Nancy,
and Rochelle lead her to believe.

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:41.519
In the movie’s final scene, Sarah’s father
can be seen packing up the car while Sarah

00:09:41.519 --> 00:09:43.620
confronts Nancy and Bonnie.

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:48.690
The year after The Craft was released, De
Young appeared in 1997's crime thriller Suicide

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:49.690
Kings.

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:54.190
De Young plays Marty, the lawyer to former
Mafia boss Charlie Barret, portrayed by Christopher

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:55.190
Walken.

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:58.889
When Charlie is kidnapped by a group of well-meaning
students in need of ransom money, Marty looks

00:09:58.889 --> 00:10:01.320
into his employer’s disappearance.

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:06.209
De Young has racked up an impressive who's-who
list of primetime TV drama appearances as

00:10:06.209 --> 00:10:07.209
well.

00:10:07.209 --> 00:10:12.850
He plays a lawyer on The Practice, a reporter
on the NCIS precursor JAG, a doctor on Melrose

00:10:12.850 --> 00:10:18.180
Place, and John Ramsey in the TV movie, Getting
Away with Murder: The JonBenet Ramsey Mystery.

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:22.490
Other highlights include a four-episode stint
as Agent John Bonacheck on The Young and the

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:25.529
Restless and a two-episode arc on Grey's Anatomy.

00:10:25.529 --> 00:10:30.889
De Young's most recent credit came as Joe
Logo in the mockumentary Reality Queen!

00:10:30.889 --> 00:10:35.389
The show follows London Logo, Joe’s daughter,
portrayed by Julia Faye West, who's determined

00:10:35.389 --> 00:10:38.999
to prove she's more than just a vapid celebrity
debutante and heiress.

00:10:40.429 --> 00:10:44.249
Nancy's mother, Grace Downs, is brought to
life by actor Helen Shaver.

00:10:44.249 --> 00:10:49.120
She may have lousy taste in men, but she seems
to luck out when it comes to their deaths.

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:53.760
Despite the uncanny circumstances surrounding
her late husband's passing, Grace is too busy

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:58.309
living the good life to worry about things
like mysterious life insurance policies

00:10:58.309 --> 00:11:02.809
Shortly after The Craft hit theaters, Shaver
appeared in the direct-to-video sequel Tremors

00:11:02.809 --> 00:11:03.809
2: Aftershocks.

00:11:03.809 --> 00:11:08.459
She took on the role of Dr. Kate Reilly, a
geologist whose field work brings her in close

00:11:08.459 --> 00:11:14.180
proximity to the Graboids, a species of subterranean
creature that's terrorizing a Mexican oil

00:11:14.180 --> 00:11:15.270
field.

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:19.750
After original Tremors character Fred Ward,
portrayed by Earl Bassett, saves Dr. Reilly’s

00:11:19.750 --> 00:11:22.259
life, she becomes his love interest.

00:11:22.259 --> 00:11:26.720
That same year, Shaver landed a main cast
role in Poltergeist: The Legacy, playing Dr.

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:29.410
Rachel Corrigan for four seasons of the horror
series.

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:33.939
Rachel, a skilled psychiatrist, is invited
to join the titular secret occult society

00:11:33.939 --> 00:11:39.050
after receiving their aid, though her cynicism
keeps her from believing in the paranormal.

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:42.509
Shaver also appeared in the 2007 indie drama
Numb.

00:11:42.509 --> 00:11:46.350
She plays Audrey, the mother to depressed
screenwriter Hudson Milbank, portrayed by

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:50.779
Matthew Perry, whose spiral of detachment
leads him to seek psychiatric help.

